# Payload branch (fhf-docs) — allowlist, not a blocklist.
#
# This branch carries the FHF documentation payload and nothing else. It is checked out at the
# workspace root, where it sits beside the lane repositories, the application-spec checkout, the
# generated harness projection and a dozen unrelated sibling checkouts — none of which belong here.
#
# Why an allowlist: with a blocklist, every new sibling repository someone clones into the
# workspace shows up as untracked, and a single "commit all" sweeps it in. That is not
# hypothetical. Commit 7454da2, "checkpoint before checking out main", added twelve sibling
# repositories to this branch as accidental gitlinks and had to be reverted; at the time of
# writing the workspace held 1.7M lines of untracked content sitting one click away from the same
# mistake. An allowlist makes the safe thing automatic: a new sibling is ignored by default, and
# adding real payload takes a deliberate un-ignore line.
#
# ADR-0018 recorded that .gitignore "stays excluded — it is harness-managed local scaffolding".
# That held while the workspace had no remote and nothing here was versioned. This branch now has
# one, so the protection belongs in the branch rather than in one machine's .git/info/exclude,
# which no clone inherits.

# Ignore everything by default.
/*

# Un-ignore the payload itself.
!/docs/
!/.gitattributes
!/.gitignore

# Generated and runtime evidence inside docs/ stays out: it is regenerated, not authored.
/docs/evidence/*.json
/docs/evidence/*.html
/docs/evidence/app-structure.md
/docs/evidence/knowledge-index.md
/docs/evidence/traceability/
/docs/evidence/current-sprint.json
/docs/evidence/spec-delta-proposals.md
/docs/evidence/qa-workflow-state.json
/docs/evidence/qa-command-center.*
/docs/evidence/teamwork-graph-enrichment.json
/docs/evidence/confluence-enrichment.json
/docs/evidence/*.json.lock
/docs/evidence/*.*.tmp
/docs/evidence/*.*.bak

# These two are engine-owned ADRs, versioned in the harness repository. Byte-identical copies were
# left at the workspace root by a branch switch. Named individually on purpose: docs/adr/ also
# holds real payload (0005-per-module-command-wrappers.md), so ignoring the directory would hide
# any future payload ADR.
/docs/adr/0024-module-chain-coverage-mode.md
/docs/adr/0025-agent-loop-instrumentation-and-memory.md
